<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wim Kok</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a>–<a href="/years/2018">2018</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wim Kok was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> trade union leader and Labour politician who served as Prime Minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> from 1994 to 2002. A co-architect of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wassenaar-agreement">Wassenaar Agreement</a> as union leader, he led two 'purple' coalitions of social democrats and liberals, without the Christian Democrats for the first time in decades. His government resigned in 2002 after a report on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srebrenica">Srebrenica</a> massacre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wim-kok.jpg" alt="Wim Kok" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rijksoverheid.nl · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wim_Kok_1994.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
